MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
RERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=13
DESCRIPTION=FL-03 (#391): add the KeyQuorum monitor system calls FL_SYS_KQ_CHECK (10), FL_SYS_KQ_VERIFY (11) and FL_SYS_KQ_HISTORY (12). syscall.c holds only a registered function-pointer table (fl_syscall_set_kq_ops, like fl_net_server_set_kq_hook), so a build with no KeyQuorum hook, or a NULL argument, answers -1; a KeyQuorum refusal is returned as -(100 + fl_kq_cp_result_t) so it never collides with -1. The KeyQuorum side (kernel/core/vfs/kq_syscall.c, fl_kq_syscall_install, called from the shell's main) only calls the existing fl_kq_cp_* checkpoints; the one new checkpoint is fl_kq_cp_verify(path), a path-based wrapper over the driver's verify. FL_SYS_KQ_CHECK validates the fl_kq_op_t and the container (fl_kq_pre_mutation is declared but not yet defined on develop, so FL-09 will swap the gate in). The VM bridge translates guest path and buffer arguments for the new numbers (vm_sys_arg_to_host_cstr, bounded to VM_SYS_PATH_MAX, refusing an unterminated or out-of-RAM string). Tests: test_kq_syscalls in tests/test_kq_checkpoint.c and a guest-path case in tests/test_vm_syscall_bridge.c. Docs in docs/FILE_SHARING_KEYQUORUM.md.

RELEASE_DATE=2026-11-17
